  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1250 AM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nMoisture levels remain elevated in the upcoming workweek with PWATs \nsitting near the 75th percentile for this time of year (1.7 to 1.9 \ninches) in the eastern half of the region. This is influenced by a \nTUTT low and weak inverted troughing that advances west over the \nnorthern Gulf towards Texas from Sunday into Labor Day. This and a \npersistent light to moderate southeasterly onshore flow helps to \npromote daily chances of isolated to scattered sea breeze rain \nshowers and storms for areas east of the I-35 corridor over the \nCoastal Plains. Elsewhere, chances through the week are quite \nminimal. Above average heat will continue with highs in the mid 90s \nto near 100 degrees and elevated heat indices that reach into the \n103 to 108 degree range for many along and to the east of I-35. \nOvernights stay warm and humid as well in the low to mid 70s.",
